00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:44.450
because you can synthesize
them on machine,

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:45.930
which makes them very cheap.

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:48.350
- Didn't you say like some people

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:49.979
have these machines at their homes?

00:16:49.979 --> 00:16:52.400
- Yeah, I'm aware of some
people that have them

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:54.779
and they're making them at
home and injecting themselves.

00:16:54.779 --> 00:16:56.370
I don't recommend that.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:17:00.770
That's currently, that's
off label use of drugs

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:03.080
and you don't want to do that,
but that gives you an idea

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:05.440
how it possible it is to
make a drug these days,

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:06.680
especially these peptides.

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:11.612
- Because there are at this
point, so easy to synthesize,

00:17:11.612 --> 00:17:14.760
and because they're relatively cheap,

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:19.230
and because they are relatively non-toxic,

00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:21.340
there's been lots and
lots of clinical studies

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:23.320
on the use of peptides.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.153
- Right.

00:17:24.153 --> 00:17:25.960
Thousands of human studies.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:27.658
And it's interesting.

00:17:27.658 --> 00:17:28.898
Why are they so safe?

00:17:28.898 --> 00:17:30.280
Well, they're not foreign.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.640
They're typically already
found in the body,

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:34.510
and they're small, so
they don't typically have

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:36.950
an immune reaction, though
the risk is not zero.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.430
- They're metabolized quickly.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:39.950
- They're also metabolized quickly.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.850
And so that the risk is relatively low,

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.795
and for that reason, there
