00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:11.122
not an abundance mimetic.

00:18:11.122 --> 00:18:12.890
- Okay, let's talk about some of these

00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:15.914
we have discussed in the past, MOTS-C.

00:18:15.914 --> 00:18:16.920
- Right.

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:17.753
- MOTS-C.

00:18:17.753 --> 00:18:18.586
- MOTS-C.

00:18:18.586 --> 00:18:19.678
So M-O-T-S dash C.

00:18:19.678 --> 00:18:21.624
That's a really interesting peptide,

00:18:21.624 --> 00:18:24.580
an unusual class that
actually doesn't come

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.620
from the nucleus, that normal chromosomes

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:27.510
that we talk about,

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:30.160
but from the mitochondrial
DNA in mitochondria,

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:32.590
and up until about 10 years ago,

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:34.173
we thought that there were only 13 genes

00:18:34.173 --> 00:18:36.330
encoded in the mitochondrial genome,

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:37.974
and there are now about a hundred known

00:18:37.974 --> 00:18:41.620
and MOTS-C is probably the
